# aliprehook commands.map: run a different command line per project
# behind the same name. Only for names defined with aliprehook_define (or
# hand-written functions using aliprehook_command).
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated, then the rest of the line):
#   project_key  command  what runs (shell syntax)
#
# Get the key for the current directory with: aliprehook key
# No line for this project -> the aliprehook_define command runs (the default).
# No `*` key here: change the default in aliprehook_define instead.
# Your arguments are appended, unless the line uses "$@" itself.
# Keep this file writable only by you (chmod go-w), or it is refused.
#
# Examples:
# github.com/org/sample_app_web  Dbuild  DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 REVISION=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD) docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml build
# github.com/org/legacy_app      Dbuild  make docker-build
# github.com/org/sample_app_api  Test    pytest "$@" -m "not slow"
